message: "If you use this software or these results, please cite them as below."
title: "target-mixup-core: code, derived results and pre-specification records for a staged study of target mix-ups in AI-assisted lung CT analysis"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Institute-of-One/target-mixup-core"
authors:
  - family-names: Yamamoto
    given-names: Shuji
    affiliation: "Institute of One, LISIT Co., Ltd., Tokyo 150-0044, Japan"
    email: yamamoto@lisit.jp
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9211-1071"
keywords:
  - target identification
  - AI agents
  - DICOM segmentation
  - lung nodule
  - double reading
  - request verification
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, derived results, freeze records and protocol documents for a three-stage study of where target
  mix-ups arise in AI-assisted imaging analysis: a census of public lung CT DICOM segmentations, a controlled gate
  experiment, and expert requests in three hash-frozen sets with a blinded lobe adjudication. No images are included.
